      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-285119",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the equations $5x - 2y = 1$ and $mx + ny = 1$, where $m$ and $n$ are constants. The graphs of these equations in the $xy$-plane represent perpendicular lines. Which of the following pairs of equations also represents a pair of perpendicular lines?\n\n1. $5x + 2y = 1$ and $mx - 3ny = 1$\n2. $5x + 2y = 1$ and $mx - ny = 1$\n3. $10x - 4y = 1$ and $2mx + ny = 1$"
